+/*
+ * TB710FU: incremental, quiescent switch programming.
+ *
+ * Upstream clears every switch (AUX, DPDM, SENSE, MIC, AGND), restarts the
+ * audio FSM and re-arms both MG bias boosters on each call, then rebuilds the
+ * requested state.  The vendor driver never does that: it keeps a cached
+ * switch mask and only updates the one group that changed.
+ *
+ * On this board the difference is fatal in a very specific way: closing the
+ * AUX analog switch while the sink is already powered and driving SBU (a hot
+ * re-plug after a DP session) hard-resets the SoC.  AUX and DPDM are
+ * therefore enabled once, at probe (cold), and kept routed for the lifetime
+ * of the driver; a re-plug never has to close them again.
+ */
